title:: BMMasterFader
summary:: Documentation BEASTmulch - a master fader for a server
categories:: Classes

Description::

See also: link::Classes/Root Classes/BMAbstractAudioChainElement::, link::Classes/Root Classes/BMMasterFaderGUI::

CLASSMETHODS::

method:: new
Create a new master fader.

argument:: target
Target for this object's Group. If target is not a Group or Synth, it will be converted as follows: If it is a Server, it will be converted to the default_group of that server. If it is nil, to the default group of the default Server. Note: A Synth is not a valid target for code::\addToHead:: and code::\addToTail::.
argument:: addAction
one of the following Symbols:		
code::\addToHead:: - add at the head of the group specified by target
code::\addToTail:: - (the default) add at the tail of the group specified by target
code::\addAfter:: - add immediately after target in its server's node order
code::\addBefore:: - add immediately before target in its server's node order
code::\addReplace:: - replace target and take its place in its server's node order
argument:: name
A Symbol indicating the name of this object. If not supplied one will be generated.


INSTANCEMETHODS::
	
method:: maxLevel
Set or get the maximum level in dBFS for this object. Default value is 0.
				
method:: level
Set or get the level in dBFS for this object. Default value is -12.
				
method:: busIndex
Get this object's control bus index.
				
method:: minLevel
Set or get the maximum level in dBFS for this object. Default value is -inf.
		
		
method:: mappings	
Set or get this object's mappings. This should be a Dictionary in the form of [\level->dBFSLevel].
		
argument:: dict		
	

method:: gui
Create and return a BMMasterFaderGUI using the receiver.


method:: free
Cleanup this object's resources.


Examples::

code::
f = BMMasterFader.new;
g = f.gui;
f.level = -6;
g.close; f.free;
::
